WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
We fetch whatever a stranger names.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.700
Including addresses only we can reach.

3
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.100
Guaranteed, not hypothetical.

4
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.500
Checking an address is not enough.

5
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:18.300
The client resolves again. So we pin it.

6
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.600
And every address, not the first.

7
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.400
One public, one loopback, is an attack.

8
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.700
A redirect is a new URL from the same stranger.

9
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.100
Every hop starts the checks again.

10
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.600
Robots is a commitment, not a risk.

11
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.100
A site that is unwell is left alone.

12
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.400
The guard is covered completely.

13
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:47.000
Pure code. No network to test around.

14
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.700
You can watch it decide.

15
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.600
One command, three answers.

16
00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:55.300
Fetching is now safe to build on.
